thon -m pytest -q tests/test_lifespan.py tests/test_plugins.py`). It gives 157 passed and 4 skipped.\n\nThe changes, in `datasette/app.py`, `datasette/utils/asgi.py` and `datasette/cli.py`:\n- **Startup entry point:** `Datasette._startup_sequence()` is idempotent and lock-guarded, and `Datasette.app()` and `serve` all go through it.\n- **Lifespan:** `AsgiLifespan` now runs startup and reports a startup exception as `lifespan.startup.failed`. Shutdown works the same way with `lifespan.shutdown.failed`.\n- **First-request fallback:** `AsgiRunOnFirstRequest` takes a lock, passes lifespan scopes straight through, and sets `_started` only after the hooks finish.\n\nI didn't run the rest of the test suite, only the spec's command.\n\nThe model flagged three concerns, and I left them alone because the spec doesn't cover them:\n- **Retry after a failed precompute:** `_setup_db_done` is only set after the whole precompute loop finishes. A `table_counts` error therefore leaves it false and the next call retries the precompute, so the model's worry doesn't match the code.\n- **No shutdown after a failed startup:** after `lifespan.startup.failed`, `AsgiLifespan` returns without waiting for a shutdown message. That matches the spec.\n- **Startup hook that calls the app:** the first-request lock could deadlock if a startup hook sends a request back into the app on a host that never sends lifespan events (such as `ds.client`). I didn't test this.", "ttft_ms": 3417, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 96870, "uuid": "f63181e6-83c6-4cac-84ce-bc1e6f6627b1", "ttft_stream_ms": 2454, "time_to_request_ms": 50, "first_content_frame_ms": 2454, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
